course: dictionary
lesson: 5733
title: Winners, losers and name-calling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A loser is a person or team that does not win a game, race or competition. Every match has a winner and a loser, so losing is a normal part of playing. «Chloe switches the dance game off mid-song when she's losing to Aisha, then later texts: "sorry, I was being a sore loser".» A sore loser gets cross and sulks when they lose.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is being used. After an election, «the loser usually congratulates the winner», so loser means the person who did not win. A good loser is different: they shake hands and say «well played», even when losing hurts.
explain: The word can also be a rude insult. Calling someone a loser to make them feel small, or to make them feel they are not cool, is name-calling and it is hurtful. Ask yourself: is this sentence about a game, or is it about a person being insulted?
fact: A loser is a person or team that loses a game, race or competition.
fact: A «good loser» shakes hands and says «well played», instead of sulking.
fact: A «sore loser» or «bad loser» gets cross and sulks when they lose.
fact: Calling someone a «loser» to hurt them is rude slang and name-calling.
fact: Losers still matter: after an election, the loser usually congratulates the winner.
exercise: «sorry, I was being a sore loser» means what? | A team that came second in the league | *Someone who gets cross and sulks when they lose | A player who has hurt their arm | Someone who wins every single game
exercise: What is a good loser? | A person who never plays any games | A person who sulks and throws the cards | *A person who shakes hands and says well played | A person who calls the winners names
exercise: Which use of loser is an unkind insult? | The loser of the race sat down on the grass | The team that lost the final | The person who did not win the vote | *Calling a classmate a loser to make them feel small
test: Mia says «well played» after losing the spelling bee. What kind of loser is she? | A cheating loser | A sore loser | *A good loser | A loser who shouts
test: In «the loser usually congratulates the winner», what does loser mean? | A rude name for someone | A person who cheats | *The person or team who did not win | A player who is hurt
exam: Which phrase means someone who shakes hands and says well played when they lose? | sore loser | *good loser | losers weepers | bad loser
